'''Zuffa Boxing''' is a [[professional boxing]] [[Promoter (entertainment)|promotion company]] founded by CEO of the [[Ultimate Fighting Championship]] (UFC), [[Dana White]], and Chairman of the [[General Entertainment Authority|Saudi Arabian General Entertainment Authority]] (GEA), [[Turki Al-Sheikh]]. The company is a [[joint venture]] between [[Sela (company)|Sela]] and [[TKO Group Holdings]] (TKO), and is based in [[Las Vegas]], [[Nevada]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnston |first=Mike |date=2025-03-05 |title=Dana White, Turki Alalshikh announce new TKO Group boxing organization |url=https://www.sportsnet.ca/ufc/article/dana-white-turki-alalshikh-announce-new-tko-group-boxing-organization/ |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=Sportsnet.ca |language=en}}</ref>

The promotion had its inaugural event, a fight between [[Canelo Álvarez vs. Terence Crawford|Canelo Álvarez and Terence Crawford]], on September 13, 2025, at [[Allegiant Stadium]] in [[Paradise, Nevada]].<ref name=SaudiSeason>{{Cite web |title=CANELO ÁLVAREZ TO FACE TERENCE CRAWFORD IN BLOCKBUSTER RIYADH SEASON SHOWDOWN SATURDAY, SEPTEMBER 13 IN LAS VEGAS, STREAMING LIVE GLOBALLY ON NETFLIX |url=https://www.ufc.com/news/canelo-alvarez-face-terence-crawford-blockbuster-riyadh-season-showdown-saturday-september-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250723125644/https://www.ufc.com/news/canelo-alvarez-face-terence-crawford-blockbuster-riyadh-season-showdown-saturday-september-13 |archive-date=July 23, 2025 |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=UFC |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref>

==History==

In August 2017, following the high-profile boxing match between [[Mixed martial arts|MMA]] fighter [[Floyd Mayweather Jr. vs. Conor McGregor|Conor McGregor and boxing champion Floyd Mayweather Jr.]], [[Dana White]] announced his intention to enter the world of [[professional boxing]] under the "Zuffa Boxing" brand.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-11-08 |title=UFC prez White seeks boxing promoter license |url=https://www.espn.com/mma/story/_/id/21341423/ufc-president-dana-white-interested-promoting-boxing-matches |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> White suggested that the existing boxing promotion landscape was "broken" and needed a centralized, promoter-driven model similar to the [[Ultimate Fighting Championship]] (UFC), of which White was then president. Despite media attention and the sale of branded merchandise, Zuffa Boxing's launch was repeatedly delayed.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harkness |first=Ryan |date=2017-11-08 |title=Dana White: The UFC Is ‘100% Getting Into Boxing’ |url=https://www.mmamania.com/2017/11/8/16623036/dana-white-ufc-is-100-getting-into-boxing |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=MMAmania.com |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Woods |first=Michael |date=2019-10-05 |title=Dana White talks Zuffa potentially buying PBC, boxing’s ‘broken model’ |url=https://www.badlefthook.com/2019/10/5/20899912/dana-white-interview-zuffa-potentially-buying-pbc-boxing-broken-model |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=Bad Left Hook |language=en-US}}</ref>

On June 18, 2025, Dana White officially announced that the UFC's parent company [[TKO Group Holdings]] (TKO) would enter the boxing industry under the '''Zuffa Boxing''' name, reviving the brand White had originally teased in 2017. The announcement was made public through an interview with ''[[Sports Business Journal]]'' in which White reiterated that Zuffa Boxing aimed to apply the UFC's promotional model to professional boxing.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-20 |title=Callum Walsh Ready To Cash In His Ticket, Become Face Of Zuffa Boxing |url=https://ringmagazine.com/en/news/unedited-callum-walsh-ready-to-cash-in-his-ticket-become-the-face-of-zuffa-boxing |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=RingMagazine.com |language=en}}</ref> The branding of TKO's boxing venture as "Zuffa Boxing" was confirmed by additional outlets the following day.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Stern |first=Adam |date=2025-08-07 |title=Dana White: TKO’s new boxing venture to be named Zuffa Boxing |url=https://www.sportsbusinessjournal.com/Articles/2025/06/18/dana-white-tkos-new-boxing-venture-to-be-named-zuffa-boxing/ |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=Sports Business Journal |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=LaMar |first=Robert |date=2025-06-20 |title=Zuffa Boxing Is Born |url=https://dicecitysports.com/2025/06/19/zuffa-boxing-is-born/ |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=Dice City Sports |language=en-US}}</ref> 

Shortly after the announcement, it was revealed that TKO would be the lead promoter of the [[super middleweight]] fight between [[Canelo Álvarez]] and [[Terence Crawford]], scheduled for September 13, 2025, at [[Allegiant Stadium]] in [[Paradise, Nevada]]. The bout, which was streamed globally via [[Netflix]], was organized in partnership with Saudi entertainment company [[Sela (company)|Sela]] with the backing of [[Turki Al-Sheikh]], Chairman of the [[General Entertainment Authority]] of [[Saudi Arabia]]. On June 23, 2025, ''[[The Ring (magazine)|The Ring Magazine]]'' formally announced that the [[Canelo Álvarez vs. Terence Crawford|Canelo vs. Crawford]] fight would serve as the inaugural event under the Zuffa Boxing banner.<ref name=TKOBoxingSept2025>{{Cite web |last=Martin |first=Damon |date=2025-07-23 |title=TKO Boxing approved for promoter’s license in Nevada, Canelo vs. Crawford official for Sept. 13 |url=https://www.mmafighting.com/2025/7/23/24473130/tko-boxing-approved-for-promoters-license-in-nevada-canelo-vs-crawford-official-for-sept-13 |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=MMA Fighting |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=SaudiSeason/> On September 29, 2025, it was announced that Zuffa Boxing had signed a media rights agreement with [[Paramount Skydance]] for their events to air on the [[Paramount+]] streaming service with selected events to be simulcast on [[CBS]].<ref name="ZuffaParamount">{{cite web|url=https://www.ufc.com/news/paramount-announces-landmark-media-rights-deal-with-zuffa-boxing|title=Paramount Announces Landmark Media Rights Deal With Zuffa Boxing|work=[[Ultimate Fighting Championship]]|date=September 29, 2025|accessdate=September 29, 2025}}</ref> 

Zuffa Boxing's first event under the Paramount Skydance partnership, [[2026 in Zuffa Boxing#Zuffa Boxing 01|Zuffa Boxing 01]], took place on January 23, 2026 at the [[UFC Apex|Meta Apex]] in the [[Las Vegas Valley]], a day prior to [[UFC 324]].<ref name=ZB01>{{Cite web |title=Zuffa Boxing first show planned for January 23 on Paramount+ |url=https://www.boxingscene.com/articles/zuffa-boxing-first-show-planned-for-january-23-on-paramount |access-date=2025-12-11 |website=www.boxingscene.com |language=en}}</ref> On February 26, it was announced by TKO president [[Mark Shapiro (media executive)|Mark Shapiro]] that Zuffa Boxing will promote the heavyweight match between [[Tyson Fury]] and [[Arslanbek Makhmudov]], which [[Netflix]] will broadcast on April 11, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dawson |first=Alan |date=2026-02-26 |title=Zuffa to Promote Fury vs Makhmudov as White's War With Traditional Boxing Promoters Escalates |url=https://boxing-social.com/features/tyson-fury-arslanbek-makhmudov-zuffa-boxing-news/ |access-date=2026-03-01 |website=Boxing Social |language=en}}</ref>

